findings=[
 {'id':'Q330','title':'The eviction policy cycle skips the promised seven-day rung for smaller custom values','source':'crates/distillery/alembic/src/memory_levels.rs:93,99','status':'verified unchanged cycled method on matching enum fixture; full recall/kernel feature and product UI not executed','evidence':'The public method documents that an arbitrary KeepDays(n) advances to the next curated rung above n, with rungs 7,30,90,forever. Its first branch is d<30=>KeepDays(30), so every 0..6 value jumps to 30 instead of 7. The exact unchanged method reproduces this while ordinary rungs and KeepSessions fallback behave as documented. The fixture enum preserves all variants but omits serde derives; this is pure policy-method execution, not an actual persisted host setting or eviction pass. A live non-rung UI consumer was not established.','diagnostics':['ingest_helpers_probe_receipt.json'],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Add the below-seven branch or correct the advertised arbitrary-value policy. Preserve the user-owned retention policy; this finding does not authorize changing defaults.'}},
 {'id':'Q331','title':'Remote-context discovery skips nested contexts inside inline context definitions','source':'crates/graph/linked-data/src/ingest.rs:365,381,395','status':'verified exact scanner functions over retained serde_json; full JSON-LD expansion/acquisition pipeline not executed','evidence':'referenced_context_urls says it finds string references in any top-level or nested @context. collect_context_urls deliberately skips recursing into an @context value; collect_context_strings handles strings/arrays but ignores objects. Consequently a term definition containing its own @context URL is omitted, both inside a single inline context object and inside a context array. Exact original helpers return [] for the first and only the outer URL for the second. Positive controls retain top-level/@graph references and ignore ordinary IRI fields. A host using this scanner to prepare an offline cache can miss a required context, but no in-tree live acquisition consumer or actual remote/parser failure was established.','diagnostics':['ingest_helpers_probe_receipt.json'],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Traverse scoped context definitions and supported context import references without treating ordinary term IRIs as fetch requests. Keep network acquisition bounded and host-owned; parser callbacks should continue refusing missing cache entries.'}}
]
for f in findings:f['verification']=NAME
notes['findings'].extend(findings)
rows=[
 ('Alembic implementation is a recall read model, not the advertised whole workshop','Package prose describes the intended actor/workshop split, then explicitly says it has no implementation yet.', ['crates/distillery/alembic/Cargo.toml','crates/distillery/alembic/src/lib.rs','crates/distillery/alembic/src/memory_levels.rs'], 'Only memory_levels is exported behind recall. The larger Athanor/grant/actor claims are architecture, not executable features of this crate. The source names this limit rather than returning a success-shaped fake workshop result.'),
 ('Retention reads canonical content tags but keeps a separate host time map','Promotion delegates to graph.node_content_tags; KeepDays accepts a String-keyed visit map while KeepSessions reads the graph facet.', ['crates/distillery/alembic/src/memory_levels.rs','crates/system/pandect/src/persona_settings_store.rs'], 'Pinning is explicitly not retention. Eviction calculation returns IDs and mutates nothing. This is a named split timing input rather than one clock/history owner; the host must supply the right UUID strings. KeepForever test inserts literal a/b keys, which do not equal its generated UUID IDs, weakening its stale-record setup.'),
 ('Policy boundary behavior differs by time axis','Days uses visited<cutoff; sessions uses a saturating age>=threshold and leaves zero stamps undated.', ['crates/distillery/alembic/src/memory_levels.rs'], 'No time arithmetic overflow was found in the u32-day to u64-ms multiplication. Defaults are 30 days and a named description is available; this alone does not prove the UI shows policy or that an eviction pass is wired. Q330 bounds the custom-value cycle discrepancy.'),
 ('Observation admission distinguishes rejection from operation success','ObservationStore returns Admission::Retained or typed Rejected while reserving StoreError for invalid clock/sequence state.', ['crates/domain/apparatus/src/observation.rs'], 'Rejected observations consume sequence IDs and increment loss counters. Result::Ok does not mean retained, which callers must pattern-match. Envelope bytes are counted deterministically plus caller-declared encoded payload length; source explicitly disclaims allocator/export bounds and false payload accounting.'),
 ('Reader gaps have independent cursor custody','Store read clones records and advances one private Cursor; loss remains cumulative in StoreStats.', ['crates/domain/apparatus/src/observation.rs','crates/domain/apparatus/src/observation/tests.rs'], 'Count/byte/age pruning, trailing unavailable ranges and batch successors are source-tested and freshly run. Zero read leaves cursor unchanged while reporting stats/boundary. map_payload preserves original accounting instead of pretending a transformed export payload was readmitted.'),
 ('Run identity uniqueness is caller-owned beyond one reset','Store reset rejects the immediately previous run and increments its local generation.', ['crates/domain/apparatus/src/observation.rs'], 'Source explicitly avoids an unbounded prior-ID history and requires producers never to reuse a run ID. RecordRef has run/source/sequence but not local generation. Do not interpret the local increment as global uniqueness or durable-journal custody across separately constructed stores.'),
 ('Inspection display limits are separate from retention limits','inspect_batch takes copied Batch data and caller-supplied retention facts.', ['crates/domain/apparatus/src/inspection.rs'], 'It truncates displayed scalar text, reports display truncation/loss/unknown coverage separately and exposes unavailable causal fields. Payload labels are borrowed/redacted by the product, not a generic serialize-everything inspector. Structural projection deliberately supplies no bounds, focus or actions.'),
 ('Apparatus retains its old skeleton alongside actual batch inspection','Default projection includes project_skeleton and project_inspection.', ['crates/domain/apparatus/src/lib.rs','crates/domain/apparatus/src/inspection.rs'], 'The skeleton labels four empty future lanes, while batch rows now exist separately. This is obsolete scaffold beside a reusable implementation, honestly labeled pre-alpha/v0. Root path IDs are fixed; products must compose projections with their own scope/grafting policy rather than assuming one global inspector authority.'),
 ('JSON-LD and quad input share a collector but preserve a legacy lossy DTO seam','ImportEnvelope holds immutable parser evidence, while old from_* helpers discard it into GraphContribution.', ['crates/graph/linked-data/src/ingest.rs','crates/graph/linked-data/src/ingest/envelope.rs','crates/graph/linked-data/src/ingest/apply.rs'], 'apply_import uses carried assertion/definition evidence; apply_contribution follows compatibility paths without it. The two apply APIs are not equivalent ownership routes. Full remaining export/query/lib code is unread, so complete-format/round-trip claims remain unproven at this checkpoint.'),
 ('Classic reification has a cautious promotion bridge','bridge_classic_reification lifts only complete single-valued asserted descriptions, or explicitly qualified history rows.', ['crates/graph/linked-data/src/jsonld.rs','crates/graph/linked-data/src/jsonld/tests/descriptions.rs','crates/graph/linked-data/src/ingest.rs'], 'Incomplete, ambiguous, unsupported metadata and cross-graph descriptions remain RDF rather than becoming assertions. Native RDF 1.2 metadata has a deliberate compatibility path that accepts additional label/time shapes. Independent eligibility rules therefore remain beyond shared collection; tests were read, not run with OxRDF.'),
 ('Metadata vocabulary and graph-scope recipes have multiple owners','ingest defines lifecycle IRIs and maps graph names; jsonld imports the outer lib constants and converts classic records.', ['crates/graph/linked-data/src/ingest.rs','crates/graph/linked-data/src/jsonld.rs','crates/graph/linked-data/src/ingest/exact.rs'], 'The outer lib vocabulary/export owner and remaining codec are still to be read. Track repeated string constants, graph-scope mapping and persisted-kind spelling as actual unshared implementation recipes, without asserting a present mismatch from naming alone.'),
 ('Exact carried import reimplements persistence admission around the kernel','exact.rs merges property records or edits edge snapshots, reconstructs a Graph and validates assertion handles before replay deltas.', ['crates/graph/linked-data/src/ingest/exact.rs','crates/graph/linked-data/src/ingest/apply.rs'], 'This supports exact handles instead of content dedup but repeats stratum/family/kind/pair admission logic outside its owner. New carried edges copy/reload the whole snapshot per edge; imports can therefore scale with imported edges times existing graph work. Source evidence establishes the repeated work, not a measured benchmark or severity.'),
 ('Import refusal reporting is incomplete at the aggregate boundary','Exact helper false results and several graph write returns do not enter ApplyOutcome errors.', ['crates/graph/linked-data/src/ingest/apply.rs','crates/graph/linked-data/src/ingest/exact.rs'], 'edges_skipped counts missing endpoints only; false exact::import_edge is not counted there, and import_properties/append/title/tag/classification results are ignored. Existing exact tests prove helper refusal is nonmutating, not that the whole apply operation reports or rolls back all earlier writes. Trace consumers before promoting a false whole-product success finding.'),
 ('Tag-definition recognition exists in evidence and compatibility apply paths','ImportEvidence recognizes complete SKOS definitions before projection; apply_contribution has a separate fallback recognizer.', ['crates/graph/linked-data/src/ingest/envelope.rs','crates/graph/linked-data/src/ingest/apply.rs'], 'Both inspect type/prefLabel/owner with related eligibility rules. Curated tag attribution separately scans wasAttributedTo edges without scope/withdrawal filters. Whether that produces a wrong author for a live imported tag needs a complete current kernel/import counterexample, rather than assuming any RDF attribution statement owns user action authority.'),
 ('Carried edge and literal metadata are not symmetric','Resource statements retain lifecycle/basis fields; NodeProperty attachment stores the fields its own type exposes.', ['crates/graph/linked-data/src/ingest.rs','crates/graph/linked-data/src/jsonld/tests/profile.rs'], 'Literal attachment requires an asserted literal in the property index; default curated title/tag literals are promoted before that index. Some labels/basis/withdrawal data cannot enter NodeProperty. Complete-profile tests normalize through the same export owner, so inspect source/input preservation before treating self-comparison as an independent full-fidelity oracle.'),
 ('Date parsing and context discovery have narrow follow-ups','parse_xsd_datetime_ms divides signed nanoseconds before its u64 conversion; the scanner misses inline scoped contexts.', ['crates/graph/linked-data/src/ingest.rs'], 'Q331 is executed on exact original scanner code. For dates, a pre-epoch value within one millisecond can truncate toward zero before sign validation; no current time parsing build was run because retained time lacks parsing. Preserve as a source arithmetic follow-up rather than a passed full parser receipt.'),
 ('New test acceptance stays scoped to the actual compiled surface','Apparatus core and projection+serde test configurations compile fresh; ingest helper tests use exact extracted functions.', ['crates/domain/apparatus/src/lib.rs','crates/domain/apparatus/src/observation/tests.rs','crates/graph/linked-data/src/ingest.rs','crates/distillery/alembic/src/memory_levels.rs'], '18 std-only plus 22 projection/serde executions pass; these include repeated core cases, not 40 distinct tests. Four helper cases pass over exact retained serde_json, with a matching local enum fixture for cycled. No full linked-data/Alembic kernel fixtures, JSON-LD expansion/network fetch or product success run is claimed.')
]
